  "term": "narcosynthesis",
  "definition": "Narcosynthesis is a therapeutic method in which an intravenous barbiturate such as sodium amytal or sodium pentothal is used to help a person become calmer and more able to talk. It is one of the narcotherapy approaches that use these drugs as aids to the therapeutic process.",
